 three  of these the first a known cloud data  lab so cloud data lab is all about  taking in big data and turning it into  visualizations so it's a suite of tools  that will allow you to do that so again  if you have many thousands of sensors  around the world gathering geolocation  data you've got big data right how do  you want to slice and dice that data how  do you want to turn that into  visualizations and the Cloud Data lab  the idea behind that is it gives you the  tools for that and then there's the  cloud machine learning api's so again if  you've got big data and you want to  identify patterns in that data for  example the trash truck scenario that I  was talking about you know you can start  beginning to understand by training a  model to say  I don't know for example trash cans in  this town tend to fill up quicker than  trash cans in that town or they fill up  quicker during the summer than they do  in the winter or in the post-christmas  period they tend to fill up really  quickly because everybody's putting like  the wrapping paper in the boxes and  things like that so those kind of  patterns can emerge from machine  learning and again you can start  training your systems to be far more  intelligent training them off of geo  data and being able to build better apps  and build better scenarios and maybe  even build better businesses and then  the third one is the vision API and if  you're at the keynote yesterday the  vision API is now able to detect things  in video as well as in photographs it  can detect sentiment and video and it  doesn't show here it's hiding behind  Freddie's bowtie but he's actually got a  little camera on his front and this is  like a ten dollar camera and so and it's  1080p so you know a device like that on  a simple computer with a camera on it  you could start recording video you can  Gio you can get a geo code location you  can tag where that video was filmed and  then using things like the vision API  you can then even determine what's in  that video when you're filming it again  lots of great scenarios you know to  build great businesses on and you know  I'm hoping that you know today I was  talking about the company that you know  picked up trash and that's in novo and  had this innovative thing for picking up  trash what will I be talking about next  year you know there may be some people  here listening to these talks  seeing what's possible with cloud and  coming up with great scenarios maybe  even somebody in this room today or  somebody who is at the keynote today and  yesterday and you know I'd love to hear  about how you're using these api's and  how you're building on these api's that  really really build innovative scenarios  and the CTO of a novo gave gave us this  quote you know just really talking about  as the world's population is increasing  and more waste is being generated then  it's really vital to make sure that  waste collection is as efficient as  possible and how more efficient can you  get then actually waste collection on  demand as opposed to the far more  primitive way that we have of you know  your trash is picked up in a particular  day then there's the company pod and  those are the guys that make this little  device that I spoke about and you know  this device it like it has Bluetooth  sensor it has Wi-Fi and it has a 2g cell  signal so if it's on the pet scholar and  the pet goes  missing it once you ping it it will dial  home over the 2g cell signal and it will  also use the 2g circuit to sniff towers  around it sniff Wi-Fi around it'll use  the ble to scan beacons around it and it  will determine a location from that and  dial home and then it will show up on  your app and you know I just got this  the other day so my dog isn't with me  but I've been playing with it if you  want to see some of the locations that  had detected me as being in because I  have it in my pocket I can show you on  my phone later it's pretty cool and  again you know I've had a dog now for  nearly 10 years and I used to go to  Radio Shack in the Apple Store and other  places like that all the time to see if  I could get a locator for my dog because  I don't want to lose him but they were  always like almost the size of a water  bottle now because of this kind of  technology they can fit in something as  big as this and then the last one is a  doctor in demand and again using  geolocation what doctor and demand have  done very very simple but very very  innovative is that we all have primary  doctors or GPS but you know how often is  it that we need to talk to our doctor  but we have to make an appointment with  them it's a little bit like the trash  pickup scenario that we have to go  according to a schedule we have to be  able to fit into something but if we  need a doctor on demand and there are a  bunch of doctors who don't have  appointments at this moment in time we  need to know where they are they need to  know where we are  so using geolocation this company doctor  and demand have been able to match  customers with doctors so that they can  be seen by a doctor far sooner than if  they had to wait on an appointment for a  specific doctor and particularly in  large healthcare organizations where  there's a centralized database of your  healthcare it's not like this doctor is  going to be totally unfamiliar with your  medical record you can actually go see a  doctor who's very familiar with your  medical record and you can see them  sooner rather than later  so again geolocation opened up a  scenario like this and this kind of  thing probably wasn't possible you know  even three or four or five years ago and  the senior software engineer of that was  saying a direct connection between maps  between geolocation and improving  patient care now what better reason  right to be able to work on technology  like this it inspires me every day I  love working on this technology than to  be able to read a quote like that a  direct connection between what you do  and improving care for people  proving people's lives and you know  that's what I'm all about that's what  we're trying to be all about with Google  trying to be all about hearing cloud you  know improve quality of your life give  you tools give you frameworks give you  ap is that you can build something that  will improve other people's lives  whether it be tracking their pet whether  we picking up their trash whether it be  connecting them with doctors so just  with that I just want to say thank you  for being here  [Music]  you
 

